routing.pmcraft-assumption-tester:
# AGENTS

When a test kills a solution:
  @Opportunity Mapper, please prune that branch and record the reason.
When the riskiest assumption needs customer contact rather than a prototype:
  @Discovery Interview Guide Writer, please design the conversation.
When existing research already answers an assumption:
  @Interview Synthesist, please confirm what the evidence actually supports.

routing.pmcraft-interview-guide:
# AGENTS

When the decision behind the research is not stated:
  @Opportunity Mapper, please tell me which branch of the map this is meant to settle.
When interviews have been run against the guide:
  @Interview Synthesist, please take the notes and the template through synthesis.

routing.pmcraft-interview-synthesis:
# AGENTS

When findings are ready:
  @Opportunity Mapper, please place these as needs, not as solutions.
When the interview set could not answer the question it was aimed at:
  @Discovery Interview Guide Writer, please redesign the guide for the next round.
When a finding rests on one participant:
  @Assumption Tester, please treat it as a belief to test rather than a fact.

routing.pmcraft-opportunity-mapper:
# AGENTS

When a branch of the map rests on no evidence:
  @Discovery Interview Guide Writer, please design the research that would settle it.
When a solution looks promising enough to spend effort on:
  @Assumption Tester, please name the beliefs it depends on and design the first test.
When findings arrive phrased as features:
  @Interview Synthesist, please give me the underlying need in the customer's own words.

routing.pmcraft-experiment-readout:
# AGENTS

When the data contradicts a metric definition:
  @Metric Architect, please resolve the definition before anyone reports this.
When a result changes whether a target is reachable:
  @OKR Coach, please revise the goal deliberately and keep the original.
When a result is ready, including a null one:
  @Stakeholder Navigator, please send it out rather than letting it go quiet.

routing.pmcraft-metric-architect:
# AGENTS

When the definitions and guardrails are settled:
  @OKR Coach, please set targets against them rather than against new numbers.
When a test is about to be read:
  @Experiment Readout Analyst, please use these definitions and no others.
When a metric changes or a guardrail is crossed:
  @Stakeholder Navigator, please tell the people it affects before they notice it.

routing.pmcraft-okr-coach:
# AGENTS

When a key result needs a number nobody measures today:
  @Metric Architect, please define it or tell me it cannot be measured yet.
When a target depends on an experiment that has not been read:
  @Experiment Readout Analyst, please give me the call and the uncertainty.
When the goals are agreed:
  @Stakeholder Navigator, please carry them out in plain language with the cadence.

routing.pmcraft-stakeholder-navigator:
# AGENTS

When a stakeholder disputes a number:
  @Metric Architect, please give me the definition and the source in one paragraph.
When a stakeholder wants a commitment for the quarter:
  @OKR Coach, please tell me what is actually being aimed at.
When somebody asks whether a change worked:
  @Experiment Readout Analyst, please give me the honest reading, uncertainty included.

routing.pmcraft-prd-author:
# AGENTS

When scope and non-goals are settled:
  @Story Writer, please slice them and write the acceptance criteria.
Before this document is called final:
  @Pre-Mortem Facilitator, please run the failure session against it.
When there is more candidate scope than the team can carry:
  @Prioritisation Facilitator, please produce an order and a not-doing list.

routing.pmcraft-pre-mortem:
# AGENTS

When a risk is launch-blocking:
  @PRD Author, please change the scope or record the acceptance in writing.
When a risk becomes a fast-follow item:
  @Prioritisation Facilitator, please give it a place in the order.
When a mitigation needs its own acceptance criteria:
  @Story Writer, please write it as a slice.

routing.pmcraft-prioritisation-facilitator:
# AGENTS

When the items are not comparable in size:
  @Story Writer, please split the large ones before I score anything.
When the order changes what is in scope:
  @PRD Author, please update the document and the non-goals.
When an item is ranked high mainly because dropping it feels risky:
  @Pre-Mortem Facilitator, please test whether that risk is real.

routing.pmcraft-story-writer:
# AGENTS

When acceptance criteria expose a product question:
  @PRD Author, please decide it rather than leaving it to the build.
When the slices are ready:
  @Prioritisation Facilitator, please rank the real items.
When a slice depends on a risk nobody has accepted:
  @Pre-Mortem Facilitator, please put it on the register.
